# Read by `pnpm test:conformance:postgres:hosted` (after docker/postgres.env, which has DATABASE_URL,
# docker/s3.env, and docker/azurite.env, of which the run takes only the mock OIDC settings): run the
# reference server as the hosted edition on the postgres provider, with its files in a new bucket of the
# local S3 server, the local user directory and surveyjs.io sign-in through the mock OIDC server, on a new
# database for the run. See README.md.
CONFORMANCE_PROVIDER=postgres
CONFORMANCE_EDITION=hosted
CONFORMANCE_FILE_STORE=s3
